{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "Prior Approval",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single-storey rear extension, as submitted, cannot be considered permitted development under Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), because the Local Planning Authority is not satisfied that the development would be lawful by virtue of Article 3(5). Article 3(5) requires the existing use of the dwelling to be lawful; however the dwelling has been unlawfully converted to a C4 House in Multiple Occupation.\r\nNotwithstanding this, the proposal would, due to its excessive depth and proximity to the shared boundary, result in an unacceptable loss of outlook, light and an unacceptable sense of enclosure to neighbouring properties harming their living conditions contrary to Local Plan policies CC2 and SC7 and the intent of the Council's adopted Residential Extension Guidelines.\r\nAs a result, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the proposal complies with the requirements of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A. Accordingly, the development does not benefit from permitted development rights and therefore Prior Approval cannot be granted.\r\n"
  ],
